Marvel's midnight Sons is the new game  from for axis games the studio behind  civilization and the past three XCOM  titles midnight Suns is far from a  superhero reskin of XCOM however as it's  got a card based combat system and a  more substantial focus on role play  here's everything you need to know about  Marvel's midnight Suns the story in  Midnight Suns is based Loosely on the  90s comic book series rise of the  midnight Suns a crossover event that  paired up the Avengers with more  Supernatural and Magic based characters  to stop a demonic threat since the story  revolves around mystical threats the  roster includes characters who  specialize in supernatural abilities  like Doctor Strange Ghost Rider magic  and blade those characters are joined by  Avenger Mainstays like Captain America  Captain Marvel Iron Man and Wolverine at  launch there'll be 13 playable  characters with four more coming as DLC  but one of those 13 is your own player  character that character called the  Hunter is customizable in everything  from their appearance to their power set  and for axis says it worked closely with  Marvel to develop them the hunter has a  really cool Marvel tie-in too they are  the child of Lilith mother of demons  conveniently the main antagonist of the  game Lilith and her horde have joined  forces with Hydra and it's up to the  hunter to lead a team of Marvel heroes  to defeat them Marvel's midnight Sun's  combat will be turn-based similar to  XCOM 2 and XCOM Chimera Squad but with a  major twist instead of set abilities  Your Heroes will each have a deck of  ability cards that get shuffled together  when you bring three of them into combat  those cards range from basic attacks to  special skills allowing you to buff  other heroes or toss enemies around the  battlefield the cards can also be  customized with variations to suit your  playstyle in XCOM each of your soldiers  has a set of abilities they're able to  use but no guarantee that the ability  will hit this element of Random could be  thrilling a soldier hitting a shot they  had very little chance to hit for  example or disappointing like completely  whiffing a shot that had a 95 chance to  hit and believe me it's happened for the  first year of midnight Sun's development  the team at faraxis tried adding these  roles of the virtual dice to the game  and in their words they just didn't work  after experimenting with ways to  incorporate elements of Randomness into  the game they landed on a deck building  system if you don't like the cards you  wind up with you have the option to  redraw at least two of them each turn to  make sure you're never without options  your abilities come with a lot of  caveats and additional effects making  team Synergy and careful planning  extremely important for instance some  Attack cards come with the knockback  effect where the enemy you hit can be  sent flying if you crash them into an  object you can deal extra damage send  them into another character and you can  hurt both quick attacks give you an  extra card play in your turn if you you  kill the enemy you're attacking since  you can only play three cards in a turn  having quick cards can extend your  actions significantly you also need to  think about which enemies you target  since your cards will automatically move  your characters around the battlefield  which is sometimes essential to keeping  them out of Harm's Way from a coming  attack or effect but can also leave you  exposed if you're not careful playing  cards also builds up a resource called  heroism which is another key element of  your planning using your more powerful  cards requires you to spend heroism so  you want to build up your stock for  those big moments where you can do  things like Drive Ghost Rider's car  through multiple enemies or bombard the  battlefield with Iron Man's missiles but  you can also use heroism without cards  spending heroism can allow your  characters to interact with the  environment like throwing a rocket an  enemy or blowing up an explosive Barrel  if you've got enough heroism the  environment can give you what are  essentially additional attack  opportunities these special superpower  moves are unlocked by forging  relationships with other characters  while in your base of operations The  Abbey between the major plot points  midnight Suns allows you to explore  optional personal Side Stories and it's  in those smaller interactions between  the Hunter and the individual members of  their team that the game manages to  squeeze out memorable moments building  up your friendship with certain Heroes  unlocks additional cutscenes and  conversations with them many of which  culminate in heartwarming reveals or  devastating discoveries midnight Suns  tracks the flow of time in a way that's  similar to x-com limiting the actions  you can take during each in-game day at  the start of a day you wake up in the  Abbey where you can run around having  conversations with characters chasing  down Collectibles and advancing story  beats building up the base researching  new gear and interacting with a crafting  system that can earn you new cards at  some point you'll eventually pick combat  missions to take on the further in the  game you get like x-com the more  missions become available and you can  can choose to take on key Story battles  or go after more generic ones that offer  resources you might need after your  mission for the day you return to The  Abbey at night where more story unfolds  midnight Suns includes dialogue trees  that allow you to make choices about who  your Hunter is and how they react to  things and those choices can affect the  hunter standing with other characters  the game's creative director Jake  Solomon said your choices won't have big  effects on the overall narrative there  aren't multiple endings for instance but  they do affect your relationships with  the other characters and the dialogue  you might see from them the time you  spend on the story also has palpable  effects on the combat side of the game  Midnight Suns has an alignment system  for the hunter similar to what you might  see in a game like Mass Effect or  Fallout that ranges from light to dark  some dialogue responses fall into one of  the two categories adjusting your  alignment based on what you say and how  you treat people or situations but  alignment is also dictated by which  Hunter abilities you use light abilities  tend towards healing and support for  your teammates while dark abilities tend  towards dealing damage the more you use  light or dark abilities the more your  alignment shifts towards that end of the  spectrum allowing you to specialize the  hunter toward a specific combat role  while previous entries in the XCOM  series have included multiplayer  Marvel's midnight Suns is a single  player game for axis has assured fans  that it will not offer any  microtransactions that impact the  card-based battle system or gameplay in  any way there are no loot boxes and  you'll be unable to purchase the in-game  currency gamma coils to unlock more  cards you will be able to use real world  money to buy the other in-game currency  Eclipse credits but you can only use  those to buy cosmetic skins there will  be a season pass available for the game  that includes 23 premium skins as well  as four upcoming DLC Packs these pieces  of DLC each include a new hero missions  enemies skins and more the new heroes  are Deadpool X-Men's storm Venom and yes  morbius  morbin time after all midnight Suns will  launch for PC on both Steam and the epic  game store as well as on Xbox series X  and S and PlayStation 5 on December 2nd  the game is also coming to PS4 Xbox One  and even Nintendo switch but the release  date for those versions hasn't been  revealed yet there are four different  versions of midnight Suns and  pre-ordering any of them grants you the  doctor strange defender's skin first up  is the standard Edition for PC it'll  cost you 59.99 and includes the base  game which you'll get digitally then  there's the enhanced Edition for Xbox  series xns and PlayStation 5 which is  69.99 it's a physical copy of the game  that includes the base game five premium  skins as well as Xbox series and PS5  optimizations the digital plus edition  for Xbox series PS5 and PC is a digital  version of the game which includes the  base game with the next gen  optimizations as well as 11 premium  skins for 79.99 and finally there's the  legendary Edition which you can either  get in physical or digital form it  includes the base game and the season  pass which includes 23 premium skins  which you'll get at launch as well as  four pieces of DLC content which will  come at a later date if you pre-order  this Edition you get that Dr Strange  skin 30 days early and if you buy the  console version from a participating  GameStop store you'll get an Iron Man  Funko Pop the legendary edition is 99.99  for PC Xbox series and PS5 buying the  game's season pass gives you all the  content that you get in the legendary  edition we recently went Hands-On with  the game so to check out some more  gameplay as well as Jordan Remy's  Impressions make sure to click this  video and make sure to stay tuned to  Gamespot for our midnight Sun's review  which will be coming very soon thanks  for watching I'm on Twitter at Lucy  James games and I'll see you next time
 

